.TH "SERIALPORT.OPEN" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.open \- SerialPort: open() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]open()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when the port is
opened.
By default the port is opened with 8 data bits, 1 stop bit and no parity
checking.
The \f[CR]baudRate\f[R] parameter is required.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
open(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R]
An object with any of the following values:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]baudRate\f[R]
A positive, non\-zero value indicating the baud rate at which serial
communication should be established.
.TP
\f[B]bufferSize\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An unsigned long integer indicating the size of the read and write
buffers that are to be established.
If not passed, defaults to 255.
.TP
\f[B]dataBits\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer value of 7 or 8 indicating the number of data bits per frame.
If not passed, defaults to 8.
.TP
\f[B]flowControl\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The flow control type, either \f[CR]\(dqnone\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(dqhardware\(dq\f[R].
The default value is \f[CR]\(dqnone\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]parity\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The parity mode, either \f[CR]\(dqnone\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqeven\(dq\f[R], or \f[CR]\(dqodd\(dq\f[R].
The default value is \f[CR]\(dqnone\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]stopBits\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer value of 1 or 2 indicating the number of stop bits at the end
of the frame.
If not passed, defaults to 1.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Returned if the port is already open.
.TP
\f[B]NetworkError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Returned if the attempt to open the port failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Before communicating on a serial port it must be opened.
Opening the port allows the site to specify the necessary parameters
that control how data is transmitted and received.
Developers should check the documentation for the device they are
connecting to for the appropriate parameters.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] port.open({ baudRate: 9600 \f[I]/* pick your baud rate */\f[R] });
.EE
